development.question_text:
The graph shows the declining-balance value of a delivery truck that depreciates at $18\%$ p.a.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.6cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=6.6,ymin=0,ymax=66000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6},ytick={0,10000,20000,30000,40000,50000,60000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},title={Delivery truck value}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:6,samples=60]{60000*exp(x*ln(0.82))};
\addplot[only marks,blue,mark=*,mark size=1.6pt] coordinates {(0,60000) (1,49200) (2,40344) (3,33082.08) (4,27127.31) (5,22244.39) (6,18240.4)};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Read the purchase price from the graph, then use $S=V_{0}(1-r)^{n}$ to find the truck's value after $9$ years, to the nearest cent.

development.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.6cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=6.6,ymin=0,ymax=66000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6},ytick={0,10000,20000,30000,40000,50000,60000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},title={Delivery truck value}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:6,samples=60]{60000*exp(x*ln(0.82))};
\addplot[only marks,blue,mark=*,mark size=1.6pt] coordinates {(0,60000) (1,49200) (2,40344) (3,33082.08) (4,27127.31) (5,22244.39) (6,18240.4)};
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:0,60000)--(axis cs:1.6,60000);
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (axis cs:1.6,60000) {$V_{0}=\$60\,000$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$S = V_{0}(1-r)^{n}$
$=60\,000(1-0.18)^{9}$
$=60\,000(0.82)^{9}$
$=\$10\,057.17$

development.question_text:
The graph shows the declining-balance value of a refrigerated van.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.6cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=5.6,ymin=0,ymax=44000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5},ytick={0,8000,16000,24000,32000,40000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},title={Refrigerated van value}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:5,samples=60]{40000*exp(x*ln(0.8))};
\addplot[only marks,blue,mark=*,mark size=1.6pt] coordinates {(0,40000) (1,32000) (2,25600) (3,20480) (4,16384) (5,13107.2)};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Read the purchase price and the value after $1$ year from the graph, then find the annual depreciation rate.

development.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.6cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=5.6,ymin=0,ymax=44000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5},ytick={0,8000,16000,24000,32000,40000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},title={Refrigerated van value}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:5,samples=60]{40000*exp(x*ln(0.8))};
\addplot[only marks,blue,mark=*,mark size=1.6pt] coordinates {(0,40000) (1,32000) (2,25600) (3,20480) (4,16384) (5,13107.2)};
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:0,40000)--(axis cs:2.2,40000);
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:1,32000)--(axis cs:2.2,32000);
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:1,0)--(axis cs:1,32000);
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (axis cs:2.2,40000) {$\$40\,000$};
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (axis cs:2.2,32000) {$\$32\,000$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$32\,000 = 40\,000(1-r)^{1}$
$1-r=\dfrac{32\,000}{40\,000}$
$1-r=0.8$
$r=0.2$
The van depreciates at $20\%$ p.a.
